<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
	The element order follows the app store schema. The store does not validate
	this file directly, it first runs it through pre-info.xslt and validates the
	result, so unknown elements are dropped silently instead of being rejected.
	There is no element for an app to app dependency, which is why app_api is
	checked at runtime in ExAppService instead of being declared here.
-->
<info>
	<id>findling</id>
	<name>Findling</name>
	<summary>Zero-config full text search for your files</summary>
	<description><![CDATA[Findling finds the contents of your documents from the normal search bar.

This app never modifies your files, and no content ever leaves your server.

Findling needs two more things to be installed: the app "AppAPI" and the
External App "Findling Backend", which does the reading and the indexing inside
your own instance.

The first index starts on its own and runs as a background job. If this server
still uses the default AJAX cron, background jobs only run while somebody is
using the web interface, and the first index will trickle along accordingly.
Switching this instance to the system cron is the difference between hours and
weeks. "occ findling:index --status" shows how far it has come.]]></description>
	<!--
		Both halves of Findling carry the same major and minor version, so that
		nobody ends up with a companion app and a backend that disagree about
		the protocol between them. This bump to 0.2.0 is the pull queue and the
		crawl; the ExApp info.xml follows in plan 02-07.
	-->
	<version>0.2.0</version>
	<licence>agpl</licence>
	<author>street1983nk</author>
	<namespace>Findling</namespace>
	<category>files</category>
	<website>https://github.com/street1983nk/nextcloud-search</website>
	<bugs>https://github.com/street1983nk/nextcloud-search/issues</bugs>
	<repository type="git">https://github.com/street1983nk/nextcloud-search.git</repository>
	<dependencies>
		<php min-version="8.2"/>
		<nextcloud min-version="32" max-version="35"/>
	</dependencies>
	<!--
		The two blocks below sit in the order the store schema prescribes, which
		is: dependencies, background jobs, the repair block, two factor
		providers, commands. Each of them is written on one line on purpose. The
		schema pattern for a PHP class name allows no surrounding whitespace, so
		an indented class name on its own line fails the validation.

		The install step is what makes the first index start without an admin
		doing anything, which is the whole zero config promise of this app. The
		command is the way back out: it is the only way to rebuild the index
		short of uninstalling the app.
	-->
	<repair-steps><install><step>OCA\Findling\Repair\AppInstallStep</step></install></repair-steps>
	<commands><command>OCA\Findling\Command\IndexCommand</command></commands>
	<!--
		The settings block, written on one line for the same reason as the two
		above, and standing here because there is nowhere else to put it:
		IRegistrationContext has no registerSettings(), so the two classes
		cannot be registered in Application::register() the way the search
		provider and the event listeners are. Nextcloud reads these class names
		out of the installed appinfo/info.xml in AppManager::loadApp(), which
		makes this file the registration itself.

		The app store transform empties the block: pre-info.xslt has the
		templates for activity and settings swapped, so what the store
		validates is an empty <settings/>, and that passes because every child
		of the settings type carries minOccurs="0". It has no consequence,
		because the block is read at runtime from the installed file and never
		from the normalised copy the store keeps. The workflow step "State the
		settings finding explicitly" holds that finding and turns red the day
		it stops being true.

		The version stays at 0.2.0 on purpose. This plan adds no container
		route, and the joint bump of both info.xml files and the image tag
		belongs to the plan that does.
	-->
	<settings><admin>OCA\Findling\Settings\Admin</admin><admin-section>OCA\Findling\Settings\Section</admin-section></settings>
</info>
